========================================================================
SOURCE REVIEW (DE1 / DE2 — no peer edit)
========================================================================

## DE1 — `oodac/check_cap_util.oo` (already CAP-G2 shaped)

| Symbol | Role |
|--------|------|
| `sealed_fs_kind_of` | op → preferred: FsReadCap / FsWriteCap (or "") |
| `is_sealed_fs` | `sealed_fs_kind_of(name) != ""` |
| `is_soft_fs_kind` | FsReadCap / FsWriteCap (FsCap may supersede) |
| `cap_fs_granted_ok` | exact preferred OR FsCap legacy supersede |
| `cap_fs_argflow_ok` | `K:id` OR `FsCap:id` |
| `is_cap_type` | CAPS 27 incl. FsRead/FsWrite |
| `sealed_kind_of` | net first, then **fs preferred**, else legacy kinds |

Preferred map (anchors ~L129–L134):
```
read_file | fs_read | path_exists | file_size  → FsReadCap
write_file | fs_write                          → FsWriteCap
```

## DE2 — `oodac/check_caps.oo` (already CAP-G2 shaped)

Grant path (~L109–L159) uses helpers (no inverted any-granular):
```
grant_ok  = cap_net_granted_ok(kind, granted)
         || cap_fs_granted_ok(kind, granted)
has_name  = cap_net_argflow_ok(kind, cap_id, names)
         || cap_fs_argflow_ok(kind, cap_id, names)
```

This is correct **given** DE1 returns preferred FsReadCap/FsWriteCap.
Wrong-granular: bag has only FsReadCap, kind=FsWriteCap → deny.
Legacy: bag has FsCap, soft preferred → allow via supersede.
No critical hole observed under adversarial fixtures.

========================================================================
PROPERTY PROOFS (adversarial)
========================================================================

### P1 — FsReadCap alone denies write_file (check path)
- `sealed_fs_kind_of("write_file")` = `FsWriteCap`
- granted = `{FsReadCap}` → no exact, no FsCap supersede → deny `&FsWriteCap`
- Dual-repro: 2× rc=1
- Alias: `fs_write` same preferred → deny

### P2 — FsWriteCap alone denies read_file
- `sealed_fs_kind_of("read_file")` = `FsReadCap`
- granted = `{FsWriteCap}` → deny `&FsReadCap`
- Dual-repro: 2× rc=1
- Extra: `path_exists` prefers FsReadCap; FsWriteCap alone denies

### P3 — FsCap alone still allows both (legacy supersede)
- Soft preferred + bag `FsCap` → `cap_fs_granted_ok` true
- Fixture `3_fs_both_allow`: read_file + write_file under single `&FsCap` → rc=0
- Corpus `ok_fs_read.oo` / `ok_fs_write.oo` → rc=0

### P4 — Exact granular allow
- FsReadCap + read_file (free + method receiver) → rc=0
- FsWriteCap + write_file → rc=0
- FsReadCap + path_exists/file_size → rc=0
- Cross: FsReadCap ↛ write_file; FsWriteCap ↛ read_file / path_exists

